#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119539 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ce19559-0f08-5ef7-9ce4-58e8e14094ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Multiple of a Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "13fa2a8c-de7c-59ee-a838-2997494edc56" :question/math-academy-id "e-4782" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}$." :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}a &= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (-4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119540 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab0d2c2f-e7a4-51bb-a20a-f28c2f7ded8b" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Multiples of Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "1e82713d-4063-5bcd-bc2e-1d35c831ab34" :question/math-academy-id "e-4783" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nand each component of $\\mathbf{b}$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{3}a + \\frac{1}{2}b &= \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 - 2 \\\\ 2 - 3 \\\\ 4 + 1 \\\\ -3 - 4 \\\\ 1 + 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119541 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec386a91-fc52-56d8-8531-7e78a8464380" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Dot Product of Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "ba38ff28-b4f3-59b8-b18a-a278db26294d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4784" :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}$?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu \\cdot v &= u_{1} \\cdot v_{1} + u_{2} \\cdot v_{2} + u_{3} \\cdot v_{3} + u_{4} \\cdot v_{4} \\\\\n&= (-1) \\cdot (-2) + 4 \\cdot 3 + 3 \\cdot (-4) + (-5) \\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 2 + 12 - 12 - 30 \\\\\n&=-28\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119542 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94f8e0e5-8d8a-516a-8f46-d76e94305df4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Quantity in an Expression Involving the Dot Product"}] :question/id #uuid "3ec5f9d5-327b-59e5-8df7-fb37d4054021" :question/math-academy-id "e-4785" :question/problem "Let be $\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ x \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ x \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ If $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0$, find the value of $x$." :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0\n$$\n\nwe compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na \\cdot b &= 0 \\\\\n10 \\cdot x + x \\cdot x + 0 \\cdot 8 + 5 \\cdot 5 &= 0 \\\\\n10x + x^{2} + 25 &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} + 10x + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n(x + 5)^{2} &= 0 \\\\\nx &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $x=-5$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120240 :knowle